# The Debian archive the root filesystem is bootstrapped from, pinned to a
# snapshot.debian.org timestamp the generator substitutes in. A snapshot
# Release file expires about a week after it is made, so building an older
# commit needs the freshness check waived. The archive is identified by an
# exact signed timestamp and its Release signature is verified either way.
#
# TODO(snapshot-sources-upstream): a fork of the builder's own template,
# carried only because that one writes the waiver as
# `Options: check-valid-until=no` — the one-line format's spelling, which a
# deb822 file ignores in silence. Delete this file and the layer that renders
# it once the builder's template is fixed; tests/host/085 fails when it is.
X-IG-Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg
Types: deb
URIs: https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/${SNAPSHOT_ISO8601}
Suites: trixie
Components: main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
Check-Valid-Until: no

Types: deb
URIs: https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/${SNAPSHOT_ISO8601}
Suites: trixie-security
Components: main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
Check-Valid-Until: no
